<% content_for :title, "ClipRank · Explainable video ranking" %>

<main class="landing-shell">
  <section class="landing-hero">
    <div class="landing-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Real media in. Ranked clips out.</p>
      <h1>Find the strongest moments in a recording without pretending to predict virality.</h1>
      <p class="landing-lede">
        ClipRank transcribes uploaded video, builds distinct candidate clips, measures semantic,
        audio, visual, and structural signals, then renders a private Top 5 for human review.
      </p>
      <div class="landing-actions">
        <%= link_to "Owner log in", login_path, class: "button" %>
        <% if signups_enabled? %>
          <%= link_to "Try it locally", signup_path, class: "button button-secondary" %>
        <% end %>
        <%= link_to "View the source", "https://github.com/wajeeh-alam/cliprank", class: "landing-source-link", target: "_blank", rel: "noreferrer" %>
      </div>
      <% unless signups_enabled? %>
        <p class="landing-access-note">The hosted demo is invitation-only to protect transcription capacity and private media.</p>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <aside class="pipeline-card" aria-label="ClipRank processing pipeline">
      <p class="pipeline-label">Durable processing pipeline</p>
      <ol>
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Transcribe</strong><small>Timestamped Faster Whisper segments</small></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Analyze</strong><small>32 measured pre-publication signals</small></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Rank</strong><small>Versioned score with evidence</small></div></li>
        <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Render</strong><small>Private MP4 and thumbnail artifacts</small></div></li>
        <li><span>05</span><div><strong>Review</strong><small>Human-approved copy and publishing</small></div></li>
      </ol>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-section" aria-labelledby="proof-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Verified local smoke test</p>
    <h2 id="proof-heading">One real upload, observed end to end</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">These are pipeline outputs from a 31.667-second H.264/AAC recording, not fixture or canned results.</p>
    <dl class="proof-grid">
      <div><dt>14</dt><dd>transcript segments</dd></div>
      <div><dt>5</dt><dd>distinct candidates</dd></div>
      <div><dt>5</dt><dd>persisted scores</dd></div>
      <div><dt>10</dt><dd>ready media artifacts</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-section" aria-labelledby="design-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Designed for honest iteration</p>
    <h2 id="design-heading">A ranking system that keeps its claims bounded</h2>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Explainable baseline</h3>
        <p>The production score is a deterministic content-readiness heuristic with frozen weights and stored component evidence.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Shadow means shadow</h3>
        <p>Feedback models can record comparison scores, but cannot reorder clips until real time-valid outcomes pass explicit gates.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Private media</h3>
        <p>Authentication and ownership checks protect results; production playback uses short-lived URLs into a private object store.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Retry-safe jobs</h3>
        <p>PostgreSQL locks, idempotency keys, unique constraints, and completion barriers keep background retries from duplicating state.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="architecture-strip" aria-label="Production architecture">
    <div><span>Control plane</span><strong>Rails + Solid Queue</strong></div>
    <div><span>Media intelligence</span><strong>FastAPI + Whisper + FFmpeg</strong></div>
    <div><span>Durable state</span><strong>PostgreSQL + private object storage</strong></div>
  </section>
</main>
